.TH TTY "1" "2026-07-28" "BNU 9.11" "BNU Commands"
.SH NAME
tty \- print the file name of the terminal connected to standard input
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tty
[\fI\,OPTION\/\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.\" This page is derived from GNU Coreutils documentation.
This page documents BNU, an independent Bun implementation compatible with
GNU Coreutils 9.11.
.PP
Print the file name of the terminal connected to standard input.
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#tty-s'\fB\-s, \-\-silent, \-\-quiet\fP\X'tty: link'
print nothing, only return an exit status
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/tty#tty--help'\fB\-\-help\fP\X'tty: link'
display this help and exit
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/tty#tty--version'\fB\-\-version\fP\X'tty: link'
output version information and exit
